## 2. Project Overview

YEAST Artisan Bakery & Grocer is a website project designed to introduce
a bakery and grocery business to online visitors. The website provides
information about the business, displays its products, and gives
visitors ways to make enquiries and find contact information.

The website is built using HTML, CSS and JavaScript where applicable.
Its files are separated into pages, styles, images and JavaScript
folders to make the project easier to navigate and maintain. Responsive
CSS techniques are used to improve the experience on desktop, tablet and
mobile screens.

## 3. Website Goals and Objectives

The main goal is to create an attractive, accessible and easy-to-use
website for YEAST Artisan Bakery & Grocer.

The objectives are to: - Introduce the business and provide relevant
information. - Present bakery products and grocery offerings clearly. -
Provide consistent navigation between pages. - Allow visitors to make
enquiries. - Display contact information for visitors who want to
contact the business. - Use responsive layouts that adapt to different
screen sizes. - Keep the code and project files organised and
maintainable.

## 4. Website Pages and Key Features

-   **Home (`index.html`):** Introduces the business and provides
    navigation to key sections.
-   **About Us (`about.html`):** Provides information about the
    business.
-   **Products (`products.html`):** Displays the products offered by the
    business.
-   **Enquiry (`enquiry.html`):** Provides an enquiry form or enquiry
    interface. Only describe submission as functional if it has been
    tested successfully.
-   **Contact (`contact.html`):** Provides contact information for
    visitors.

### Technical features

-   Shared CSS styling through `styles/common.css`.
-   CSS Flexbox for arranging header and navigation content.
-   CSS Grid for product and content cards.
-   Media queries for tablet and mobile layouts.
-   Responsive image rules to help images fit different screen sizes.
-   JavaScript for form validation or interaction where implemented.
-   Separate folders for images, styles and JavaScript files.

